From: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:04:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/26] [M156] Defer HTMLPlugInElement image loads from style
 recalc to a task

Original change's description:
> Defer HTMLPlugInElement image loads from style recalc to a task
>
> Previously, HTMLPlugInElement::CustomStyleForLayoutObject() invoked
> ImageLoader::UpdateFromElement(kUpdateNormal) directly during style
> recalculation. When an <object> or <embed> transitioned to an image
> type with a cached broken or immediate image resource, ImageLoader took
> the synchronous load path inside style recalc, synchronously firing
> error events or triggering HTMLObjectElement::RenderFallbackContent()
> and DetachLayoutTree() while the style engine was in the middle of
> recalculating style.
>
> Add ImageLoader::kUpdateFromTask (guarded by
> HTMLPlugInDeferStyleRecalcImageLoad) to post the image load update as a
> DOM manipulation task while keeping the document load event delayed
> until the task runs, and update
> Document::InitiateStyleOrLayoutDependentLoadForPrint() to also wait on
> IsDelayingLoadEvent().
>
> Fixed: 575053155
> Bug: 575053155
> Change-Id: I55acfa7c5a7331248fd396776f51679064f2bf85
